hadiths[61]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1335","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) saw ‘Atard al-Taymi in the market with a silk garment (for sale), and he was a person who used to go to kings and receive money from them. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): O Messenger of Allah! I saw ‘Atard with a silk garment in the market; if you buy it and wear it when the Arab delegations come, it would be appropriate. The narrator said: I think he also said that you could wear it on Fridays as well. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Only he will wear silk in this world who has no share in the Hereafter. Then, after that, some silk garments came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he gave one garment each to Sayyiduna Umar, Usama bin Zayd, and Ali (may Allah be pleased with them all), and said: Tear it and make headscarves for your women. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) brought his garment and said: O Messenger of Allah! You sent this garment to me, and just yesterday you said what you said about ‘Atard’s garment? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I did not send this garment to you for your own wearing, but so that you may benefit from it (by selling it). And Sayyiduna Usama (may Allah be pleased with him) wore his garment and went out, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked at him in such a way that he realized the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was displeased. He said: O Messenger of Allah! Why do you look at me? You are the one who sent this garment to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I did not send it to you so that you wear it yourself, but so that you tear it and make headscarves for your women."
"1336","Khalifah bin Ka'b Abu Dharr reports: I heard Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) while he was delivering a sermon, saying: O people, beware! Do not clothe your women in silk garments, for I heard Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Do not wear silk, for whoever wears it in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"1337","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: A silk cloak was presented as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he wore it and performed prayer in it. After finishing the prayer, he took it off forcefully, as if he disliked it, and then said: ""This is not suitable for the pious."""
"1338","Abu Uthman says that Syedna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote to us while we were in Azerbaijan (a country in Iran): ""O Utbah bin Farqad, the wealth that is with you is neither earned by you, nor by your father, nor by your mother. So let the Muslims enjoy it in their places just as you enjoy it in your place (i.e., deliver it to them without them asking). And avoid living luxuriously, and avoid the ways of the polytheists, and also avoid wearing silk clothes—except this much."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his middle and index fingers and joined them together (i.e., if there is a border of two fingers' width, it is permissible). Zuhair said to Asim, ""This is what is in the book,"" and Zuhair raised both his fingers."
"1339","It is narrated from Suwaid bin Ghaflah that when Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon at (the place of) Jabiyah, he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing silk (silken cloth), except (that) it be equal to two fingers, or three, or four fingers (in width)."
"1340","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) once wore a silk cloak which had been gifted to him. Then he immediately took it off and sent it to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him). The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! You have taken it off?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Jibreel has forbidden me."" Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) weeping and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! You gave me something which you disliked; what will become of me?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I did not give it to you to wear, but rather so that you may sell it."" Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sold it for two thousand dirhams."
"1341","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) permitted Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf and Sayyiduna Zubair bin Al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with them both) to wear silk shirts during a journey, because they had developed itching or some other illness. In another narration, it is mentioned that both of them had complained of lice."
"1342","It is narrated from Abdullah, who was the freed slave of Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both) and the maternal uncle of the son of Ata, that he said: Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) sent me to Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) and told me to say: I have heard that you declare three things to be forbidden: one is a garment with silk embroidery, the second is an argwan (i.e., a bright red) saddlecloth, and the third is fasting for the entire month of Rajab. So Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: Who says that fasting in the month of Rajab is forbidden? Whoever fasts continuously (Abdullah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to fast continuously except on the two Eids and the days of Tashreeq, and his opinion was that perpetual fasting is not disliked). And as for what you mentioned about garments with silk embroidery, I heard Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Silk will be worn by the one who has no share in the Hereafter."" So I feared that embroidered garments might also be silk. And as for the argwan saddlecloth, Abdullah's own saddlecloth is argwan. I conveyed all this to Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her), and she said: The cloak of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) is present here. Then she brought out a Tayalisi Kisrawani cloak (which was attributed to the Persian king Kisra), which had silk on its collar and its hem was also of silk. Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) said: This cloak remained with Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) until she passed away. When she died, I took this cloak, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wear it. Now we wash it and give its water to the sick for healing. (A silk border up to four fingers' width on the hem is permissible; more than that is forbidden.)"
"1343","It is narrated from Amir al-Mu'minin, the rightly guided Caliph, Sayyiduna Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the king of Duma, Ukaydir, sent a gift of a silk garment to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave it to me and said: Tear it and make headscarves for the three Fatimas (one for Sayyida Fatima [may Allah be pleased with her], one for Fatima bint Asad, the mother of Sayyiduna Ali [may Allah be pleased with him], and one for Fatima bint Hamza [may Allah be pleased with her])."
"1344","It is narrated from Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing Qassi (a type of silk cloth), wearing clothes dyed with Kusum, wearing a gold ring, and reciting the Qur'an during bowing (ruku‘)."
"1345","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw me wearing two garments dyed with safflower and said, ""These are the clothes of the disbelievers, do not wear them."""
"1346","´Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade men from applying saffron and (from its color)."
"1347","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): Abu Quhafa (may Allah be pleased with him) came in the year Makkah was conquered, and his head and beard were as white as thaghamah (a type of white grass). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Change this whiteness with something, but avoid black color."""
"1348","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Jews and Christians do not dye (their hair), so you should do the opposite of them (i.e., dye your hair, but as mentioned in the previous hadith, not with black dye)."
"1349","Qatadah says that we asked Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Which garment did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) like the most?"" He replied: ""The Yemeni cloak (which is striped; this cloth is very strong and excellent)."""
"1350","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went out one morning, and he was wrapped in a black woolen cloak on which there were images of saddles."
"1351","Abu Burdah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I went to Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), and she brought out a thick lower garment that is made in Yemen and a blanket which is called a mulabbadah. Then she swore by Allah that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed away in these two garments."
"1352","´Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when I got married, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Do you have any carpets or the like?"" I replied, ""Where do we have carpets?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Soon you will have them."" Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said that my wife has a carpet; when I tell her to remove it, she says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said that soon you will have carpets. (So Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) wanted to remove them considering them disliked, because they are adornments of the world.) (""Anmaat"" refers to carpets and similar fine cloths that are spread on the ground.)"
"1353","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: One bed is for a man, one for his wife, one for the guest, and the fourth will be for the devil. (That is, the one made to show off to people and to display one's superiority.)"
"1354","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the bedding of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), on which he used to sleep, was made of leather and filled with palm fibers."
"1355","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating with the left hand, walking with one shoe, wrapping the whole body with one garment, or sitting with knees drawn up and arms wrapped around them. He also forbade exposing the private parts in a single garment (which is called Ihtiba; this is prohibited in the case where the private parts become exposed in a single garment, but if there are multiple garments or there is no fear of exposure, then it is disliked)."
"1356","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should lie on his back and then place one foot over the other."
"1357","'Ubad bin Tamim narrates from his uncle (may Allah be pleased with him) that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) lying on his back in the mosque with one leg placed over the other."
"1358","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says:` I passed in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and my lower garment was hanging down, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Abdullah! Raise your garment."" I raised it, then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Raise it higher."" So I raised it higher. After that, I would always keep my lower garment raised, until people asked, ""How high should it be raised?"" Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, ""Up to the middle of the shin."""
"1359","Muhammad bin Ziyad says: I heard from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he saw a man letting his lower garment hang down and he was striking the ground with his feet, and he was the governor of Bahrain and was saying, ""The governor has come, the governor has come."" (Upon seeing this, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty will not look at the person who lets his lower garment hang out of pride."
"1360","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: Allah Almighty will neither speak to three people on the Day of Resurrection, nor look at them (with mercy), nor purify them (from sins), and for them will be a painful punishment. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) repeated this three times, so Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: They are ruined and lost, O Messenger of Allah! Who are those people? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: One who lets his lower garment (such as izar, pajama, trousers, shalwar, etc.) hang below the ankles, the second is one who reminds others of his favors after doing them, and the third is one who sells his goods by swearing a false oath."
"1361","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty will not look at the person on the Day of Resurrection who drags his garment on the ground out of pride."
"1362","`Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: A man was walking arrogantly with his hair and garment (lower garment) showing off, eventually he was swallowed by the earth. Then he will continue sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection. (Perhaps that man was from this Ummah, but the correct view is that he was from a previous Ummah.)"
"1363","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) one morning got up silently (as if he was distressed). I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Today I have seen your blessed face in a way I have never seen before.” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Jibril (peace be upon him) had promised to meet me last night but did not come, and by Allah, he has never broken a promise.” Then the thought of the puppy that was in our tent came to his (peace and blessings be upon him) heart, so he ordered it to be removed, and it was removed. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) took water and sprinkled it where the dog had been sitting. When evening came, Jibril (peace be upon him) arrived, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “You had promised to meet me last night.” He said, “Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture.” Then, the next morning, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs, to the extent that he (peace and blessings be upon him) even had the dog of a small garden killed, but spared the dog of a large garden."
"1364","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels do not enter a house in which there are idols and pictures."
"1365","Busr bin Saeed narrates from Zaid bin Khalid, and he narrates from the companion of the Messenger of Allah, Sayyiduna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Angels do not enter a house in which there is a picture. Busr said: Zaid became ill, so we went to visit him, and there was a curtain hanging at his door on which there was an image. I said to Ubaidullah Khawlani, who was the stepson of Umm al-Mu'mineen Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her): Did not Zaid himself narrate to us the hadith about pictures? (And now a curtain with a picture is hanging.) Ubaidullah said: When he narrated it, did you not hear that he also said, ""Except for what is on cloth""?"
"1366","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to me and I had covered a niche or shelf with a curtain of mine, which had pictures on it. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw this, he tore it down and the color of his face changed, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Aisha! The people who will receive the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who make images of Allah’s creation.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said that I cut it and made a cushion or two cushions from it. (A cushion from cloth with pictures may only be made when making the cushion distorts the image.)"
"1367","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) returned from a journey and I had hung a carpet on my door, on which there were pictures of horses, so at his command, I took it down."
"1368","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she bought a cushion (the cloth on top of a mattress) which had pictures on it. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw it, he stood at the door and did not enter. I recognized that there was distress on the blessed face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I repent before Allah and His Messenger. What is my sin?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""What is this cushion?"" I said, ""I bought it for you to sit on and lean against."" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Those who make these pictures will be punished, and it will be said to them, 'Give life to what you have created.'"" Then he said, ""The angels do not enter a house in which there are pictures."" And in another narration, it is mentioned that I made two pillows from it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would rest on them in the house."
"1369","Sa'id bin Abu al-Hasan says that a man came to Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) and said, ""I am a maker of pictures, tell me about it."" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""Come near me."" He came closer. Then he said, ""Come even closer."" He came even closer, until Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) placed his hand on his head and said, ""I say to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): I heard him say, 'Every maker of pictures will go to Hell, and for every picture he made, a living being will be created for him, which will punish him in Hell.'"" And Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""If you must make pictures, then make pictures of trees or anything that does not have a soul."""
"1370","Abu Zar'ah says: I entered Marwan's house with Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and saw pictures there. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, and he used to say: Allah Almighty says: Who could be more at fault than the one who tries to create like Me? Well then, let them create a tiny ant, or a grain of wheat, or a grain of barley."
"1371","Sayyiduna Bara’ bin ‘Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us to do seven things and forbade us from seven things. He commanded us to visit the sick, to accompany funeral processions (to the grave), to respond to sneezes, to fulfill oaths, to help the oppressed, to accept invitations, and to spread or propagate Islam. And he forbade us from wearing gold rings, eating and drinking from silver utensils, (using) saddle cloths (i.e., silk saddle cloths; if they are not made of silk, then it is not forbidden), wearing Qassi (a silk cloth made in a place called Qas in Egypt), wearing silk clothes, and from Istabraq and Dibaaj (both of which are also silk fabrics)."
"1372","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a gold ring in a man's hand, so he (peace be upon him) took it off and threw it away and said: ""One of you intends a burning coal from the fire of Hell and then puts it in his hand."" When the Prophet (peace be upon him) left, the people said to that man, ""Pick up your ring and benefit from its (price)."" He replied, ""By Allah, I will never touch it after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has thrown it away."" (SubhanAllah, the piety and obedience of the Companions had reached such a level. If he had picked it up and sold it, there would have been no sin.)"
"1373","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, had a ring of gold made. When he wore it, he would turn its stone towards the palm of his hand. Then one day, he sat on the pulpit and took off that ring and said: ""I used to wear this ring and turn its stone inward,"" then he threw it away and said: ""By Allah, I will never wear it again."" Seeing this, the people also threw away their rings."
"1374","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had a ring made of silver, and it was in his hand. Then it remained in the hand of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), then it remained in the hand of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), then it remained in the hand of Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), until it fell from him into the well of Aris. The inscription on that ring was: ""Muhammad, Messenger of Allah"" (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1375","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring made of silver and had engraved on it ""Muhammad Rasul Allah"" (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to the people: I have had a ring made of silver and have had engraved on it ""Muhammad Rasul Allah"", so no one should engrave this inscription on his ring."
"1376","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to write letters to (the king of Iran) Kisra, (the king of Rome) Caesar, and (the king of Abyssinia) Najashi. The people said, ""These kings will not accept any letter unless it has a seal on it."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring made, the band of which was of silver, and ""Muhammad Rasul Allah"" was engraved on it."
"1377","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, wore a silver ring on his right hand, whose stone was from Abyssinia, and he, peace and blessings be upon him, would turn its stone towards the inside of his palm."
"1378","'Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that' the ring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on this finger, and he pointed towards the little finger of his left hand."
"1379","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade me from wearing a ring on this finger or this finger, and he pointed towards the middle finger and the one next to it. (Because these fingers are involved in every task and the ring would cause inconvenience, whereas the little finger remains separate, so it is better to wear the ring on it.)"
"1380","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a battle in which we participated, saying: Wear shoes frequently, for by wearing shoes a person remains like a rider (that is, like a rider, his feet do not suffer pain)."
"1381","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When any one of you puts on his shoes, he should start with the right foot, and when he takes them off, he should start with the left. And he should either wear both (shoes) or take off both."
"1382","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade qaza'. The narrator said: I asked Nafi' what qaza' is. He said: Shaving part of a child's head and leaving part of it."
"1383","Lady Asma bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! My daughter has become a bride and due to measles her hair has fallen out, so may I attach something to her hair? (i.e., artificial hair or similar items available in the market)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Allah has cursed the one who attaches (false hair) and the one who has it attached."""
"1384","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) strictly forbade a woman from attaching extensions to her hair."
"1385","It is narrated from Humaid bin Abdur Rahman bin Awf that he heard from Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with them both), in the year he performed Hajj. He said on the pulpit, while holding a braided lock of hair in his hand, which was with a slave: ""O people of Madinah! Where are your scholars? I heard the Messenger of Allah forbidding this (i.e., hair extensions), and he said that the Children of Israel were destroyed when their women began to do this (i.e., indulging in luxury and lust, and turning away from fighting)."""
"1386","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` Allah Almighty has cursed those who tattoo and those who get tattooed, and those who pluck facial hair and those who have it plucked, and those who widen their teeth for beauty (so that they appear beautiful and youthful), and those who alter Allah’s creation (natural form). Then this news reached a woman of the tribe of Banu Asad, who was called Umm Ya’qub and she was a reciter of the Qur’an. So she came to Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, “What is this news I have heard that you have cursed those who tattoo and those who get tattooed, and those who pluck facial hair and those who have it plucked, and those who widen their teeth, and those who alter Allah’s creation?” Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has cursed, and this is present in the Book of Allah?” The woman said, “I have read whatever is in the Qur’an in two covers, but I did not find it.” Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “If you have read it, then you must have found Allah Almighty’s statement: ‘Whatever the Messenger of Allah gives you, take it, and whatever he forbids you from, abstain from it.’ (Al-Hashr: 7)” The woman said, “Some of these things are done by your own wife.” Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Go and see.” She went to his wife but found nothing. Then she returned and said, “I did not see any of these things.” Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “If she did so, we would not live with her.”"
"1387","Lady Asma (may Allah be pleased with her) says that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""I have a co-wife. Will I be sinful if I say (to provoke her) that my husband has given me such-and-such, even though he has not given it to me?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, ""Whoever claims to have been given something which she was not given, it is as if she is wearing two garments of falsehood (and presents herself as pious and righteous, while in reality she is worldly and deceitful). There is no power and no strength except with Allah."""
"1388","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are two types of people among the inhabitants of Hell whom I have not seen. One is a people who have whips like the tails of oxen and they beat people with them. The second is women who are clothed yet naked (i.e., parts of their bodies that should be covered are exposed, such as when women wear sarees and their heads, bellies, and feet remain uncovered, or they wear clothes so tight and thin that their bodies are visible, so it is as if they are naked). They are deviated from the straight path and lead others astray, and their heads are inclined to one side like the humps of Bactrian camels. They will not enter Paradise, nor even smell its fragrance, although the fragrance of Paradise can be perceived from a great distance."""
"1389","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Bashir Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he was on a journey with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah sent a messenger. Abdullah bin Abi Bakr said: I think that messenger said this while the people were in their resting places, that there should not remain any string necklace or necklace on the neck of any camel except that it should be cut off. Malik said: I think they used to put it on to ward off the evil eye."
"1390","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany those travelers who have a bell or a dog with them."
"1391","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The bell is the musical instrument of Satan."
"1392","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade striking on the face and branding on the face."
"1393","Na'im bin Abi Abdullah, the freed slave of Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), narrates that he heard Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a donkey that had been branded on its face, and he disliked it. Ibn Abbas said: By Allah, I only brand at a place far from the face (i.e., on the thigh, etc.), and he ordered his donkey to be branded, so it was branded on the thighs. And he (Ibn Abbas) was the first to brand on the thighs."
"1394","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We went to the enclosure with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he was branding the goats on their ears."
"1395","`Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when Umm Sulaym gave birth to a child, she said to me, ""O Anas! See that this child does not eat or drink anything until you take him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the morning, and he chews something and puts it in his mouth."" Sayyiduna Anas said that then in the morning I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he was in the garden, and (from the tribe or place) he was wearing a cloak of Jawn and branding his camels which had come to him in the spoils of victory."
